────────────────────────────────────────
AUDIT LOG (K1) CONTRACT
────────────────────────────────────────

AuditLog must capture sensitive actions with consistent metadata.
Audit logs are append-only (never edited; no deletes).

Minimum required audit events (v1). Canonical names only; see docs/epics/00-NAMING-AND-PERMISSION-ALIGNMENT.md.
Tenant:
- tenant.created
- tenant.plan.assigned
- tenant.plan.changed
- tenant.billing.price_override_set
Invites/Users/Roles:
- tenant.user.invited
- tenant.invite.accepted
- tenant.invite.resent
- tenant.invite.revoked
- tenant.user.disabled (if used)
- tenant.role.changed (role assignment changes)
Requests:
- request.created
- request.closed
Evidence:
- request.evidence.file_added
- request.evidence.link_added
Approvals:
- request.approval.internal_assigned
- request.approval.external_sent
- request.approval.approved
- request.approval.rejected
- request.reminder.sent
Payments:
- request.payment.status_set
- request.payment.evidence_added
- request.payment.evidence_removed
Exports:
- request.export.pdf_generated
- request.export.bundle_generated
Comments (optional):
- request.comment.added

Rules:
1) Every audited action must include:
- actorUserId
- actorContext (TENANT or VENDOR)
- tenantId (when tenant scoped)
- action (string code)
- metadata: minimal but useful (ids, old/new, counts)

2) AuditLog visibility is permission-based:
- tenant.audit.read required

3) Do not log secrets:
- never store raw tokens (external approval tokens must be hashed in DB)
- avoid PII in metadata where not necessary
